      "description": "Watch Fulham vs AFC Wimbledon highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 27, 2026. The stage was set for a classic Carabao Cup encounter on August 27, 2026, as two teams with different ambitions met in a knockout format. Fans gathered to witness a match where every tactical move and individual effort would determine who stays in the competition. Dominant First Half Performance Fulham started the match with clear intent, pinning AFC Wimbledon back into their own half from the opening whistle. The early pressure paid off in the 37th minute when Ryan Sessegnon delivered a pinpoint ball into the danger zone, allowing Emile Smith Rowe to power home a header from very close range. The home side didn't wait long to double their advantage; in the 42nd minute, Kenny Tete turned provider with a cross that found Rodrigo Muniz , who expertly directed his header into the bottom right corner to make it 2-0. Despite the deficit, AFC Wimbledon looked to find a way back into the contest. Andy Yiadom forced a save from Benjamin Lecomte early on, and Callum Maycock missed a narrow chance, but the quality of the top-flight hosts proved difficult to overcome as the first half drew to a close. Clinical Finish and Progress The second half saw both managers turn to their benches to influence the flow of the game. Fulham introduced Macauley Zepa and Gonzalo García , while the visitors brought on Jayden Stockley to bolster their attack. The game hit a brief lull following an injury to Luc De Fougerolles , but the intensity returned in the closing stages. Nathan Bishop made several key saves to keep the scoreline respectable, denying Zepa and Kevin on multiple occasions. However, the resistance was finally broken again deep into stoppage time. In the 93rd minute, a swift break led by Macauley Zepa found Gonzalo García in space, and the substitute made no mistake with a right-footed shot into the bottom corner. The 3-0 victory marks a professional performance by Fulham , who successfully navigate this cup tie to advance further in the tournament."
